<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luis Arce</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1963</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luis Arce is a Bolivian economist and politician who was minister of economy under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evo-morales">Evo Morales</a> for most of 2006–2019 and president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a> from 2020 to 2025 for the Movement for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socialism">Socialism</a> (MAS). His presidency faced falling natural gas output, shortages of fuel and dollars, rising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">inflation</a>, a failed military uprising in June 2024 and a bitter split with Morales.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luis-arce.jpg" alt="Luis Arce" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Plurinational Legislative Assembly · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:President_Luis_Arce.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
